message: "If you use this research code, protocol records, or empirical data, please cite the archived software release: https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23641281."
title: "Building Energy Conditional Flow Matching: Six-Cohort Reliability Study"
type: software
version: "1.1.1"
date-released: "2026-11-25"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23641281"
authors:
  - given-names: "Md. Mahbubur"
    family-names: "Rahman"
    affiliation: "Department of Mechatronics Engineering, Rajshahi University of Engineering & Technology (RUET), Rajshahi, Bangladesh"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0004-0252-9140"
repository-code: "https://github.com/mahbubur2008018/building-energy-cfm-reliability"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Historical Python source code, frozen protocol configurations, baseline models, and verified aggregate
  evaluation data for a six-cohort empirical evaluation of conditional flow matching (direct,
  full residual, and no-base residual) for building energy prediction under distribution shift
  (Cairo, EDCS, Miami, BDG2, Drammen, and Oslo).
keywords:
  - "building energy estimation"
  - "conditional flow matching"
  - "probabilistic prediction"
  - "distribution shift"
  - "model reliability"
  - "uncertainty quantification"
  - "calibration"
  - "CatBoost"
  - "NGBoost"
